`pipeline_refactored.py` is written and verified. Here's what changed:

| Original problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| `DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE`, `password123` hardcoded at module level | `Config` dataclass loaded via `load_config()` from `DB_PATH`, `LOG_FILE`, `OUTPUT_FILE` env vars |
| `"INSERT INTO errors VALUES ('%s', '%s', %d)" % (...)` — SQL injection via string interpolation | Parameterized `?` placeholders via `conn.execute("INSERT INTO ... VALUES (?, ?, ?)", (...))` |
| Everything in one 118-line `proc_data()` function | 12 well-named functions across **Extract** (`parse_log_line`, `extract_logs`), **Transform** (`count_errors`, `compute_api_latency`, `compute_active_sessions`), **Load** (`init_db`, `insert_summaries`, `generate_report_html`, `write_report`), plus `run_pipeline` orchestrator |
| `line.split(" ")` with magic indices — fragile, breaks on whitespace changes | Three compiled regex patterns (`_LOG_PATTERN`, `_USER_PATTERN`, `_API_PATTERN`) with named capture groups |
| No type hints, no docstrings, no data models | Full type hints, dataclass models (`ErrorEntry`, `UserEntry`, `ApiEntry`, `WarnEntry`), docstrings on every public function |
| HTML output with `"<li><b>" + msg + "</b>: " + ...` — no escaping | `_escape_html()` helper used in report generation |

**Behavior preserved**: `report.html` output is byte-identical for the seed data. The DB schema and inserts match. Session tracking (login/logout stream processing) is identical in logic.
